From 16868bb66d0c5c73b19d76532539beb566704f70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Slivinski <sslivins@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:22:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: talkback source and /api/talk WebSocket for RTP speaker
 backchannels

Adds a talkback:rtp://<private ipv4>:<port>?codec=opus&rate=<hz> source: a
backchannel-only producer that pipes 16 kHz s16le PCM into ffmpeg (argv built
from validated fields, no shell) which sends Opus RTP to the camera, e.g. a
UniFi Protect talkback session.

GET /api/talk?src=<stream> upgrades to a WebSocket that accepts binary PCM
frames from a native client and feeds them to the stream's talkback source.
Same-host origin check, one talker per speaker, frame size and rate limits,
idle timeout and a 5 minute session cap.
